 # M1 fixture · Legacy-Style Host Plugin (0.1.1-rc.2 Era)
 
-Test fixture, **do not publish**. The content is copied verbatim from the `/tmp/demo-plugin` of the historical validation environment (legacy style written against the real interface of `@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-apiproxy@0.0.1-rc.1`); the only additions are `"private": true` in package.json and this README.
+Test fixture, **do not publish**. It started as a verbatim copy of the `/tmp/demo-plugin` of the historical validation environment (legacy style written against the real interface of `@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-apiproxy@0.0.1-rc.1`); the only additions were `"private": true` in package.json and this README. The fixture is now migrated onto the 0.1.2-alpha.2 host-plane service contract (`ctx.llm`) while keeping its documented surface: a bundle-patched host plugin that reads the LLM provider directory when it activates.
 
 Activation facts (from `benchmark/results/validation-report-2026-08-30.md`):
 
-- With this plugin attached, dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 cold boot immediately fails with `plugin tree failed ... pending (waiting for service: apiProxy)` and exit 1;
-- After migrating per the skill card (`inject: ["llm"]` + `ctx.llm.listProviders()` + removing the dead dependency), activation succeeds; with no API key in the container, a route count of 0 is expected — as long as the calls go through.
+- The pre-migration (0.1.1-rc.2-era) revision of this fixture injected the removed host
+  facade service `apiProxy` and called `ctx.apiProxy.llm.providers()`. With that revision
+  attached, dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 cold boot immediately fails with
+  `plugin tree failed ... pending (waiting for service: apiProxy)` and exit 1.
+- The fixture is migrated to the official owning domain service: `inject: ["llm"]` +
+  `ctx.llm.listProviders()`, with the dead `@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-apiproxy` dependency
+  removed. Boot-probed against dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2, activation succeeds and the provider
+  directory read goes through; with no real API key a live-provider count of 0 is
+  expected — as long as the call goes through.
